{
  "reviewer": "abstract_conclusion_consistency_auditor",
  "paper_id": "bicycle-infrastructure-paper",
  "run_status": "ok",
  "summary": "The abstract, introduction and conclusion were compared with the body, appendix and tables. The headline counts match the body: 3,187 articles, 92 relevant articles, 43 projects, 29 day- or month-dated, 14 of 15 counties, 97% pilot agreement, 700 579 listings and 38%. The summaries still overstate or omit caveats in nine places. The abstract says the data are linked to the housing listings, but the body says they have not yet been linked. The abstract says the pilot contained \"only two actual openings\", but a Table 2 footnote says a third opening was confirmed. The abstract, introduction and conclusion present the 97% pilot agreement without the body's caveat that only 3 relevant articles exist and the results are \"indicative only\". The 92-article and 43-project counts are presented as openings and projects although the full run is unvalidated and the pilot shows one LLM-flagged article that both humans coded not relevant. The conclusion says the linked data \"can support research\" on cycling behaviour and housing markets, which goes beyond the body. The abstract generalises the NVDB comparison from one case and from a single-term pilot. There is also a body-level inconsistency about the missing 2024 listing data.",
