        "text_quote": "road database NVDB shows that the articles add an exact opening date, which NVDB lacks.",
        "precision": "exact"
      },
      "claim_text": "Linking one opening to the national road database NVDB shows that the articles add an exact opening date, which NVDB lacks.",
      "assessment": "partially",
      "cannot_verify_reason": null,
      "evidence_summary": "Section 4.3 states that NVDB does not record when a road opens to traffic, only when its geometry was registered. In the single example, the geometry was registered one month before the opening. The day-level date comes from resolving 'Monday' with the publication date. The abstract's wording is scoped to one opening, but 'NVDB lacks' reads as a general finding. Section 8 says the opening dates \"should be compared systematically with NVDB registration dates and historical OpenStreetMap records, to measure how much the articles add\". The extent of the gain is therefore untested.",
